+**A wedged lane (gcp-ubv2).** When `lane-wedge.sh check` holds, the lane is
+parked: a push to the target was refused while it stood still, and nothing can
+land until it moves. The scan then takes only beads labelled `base-red`, none of
+the `skip=` ids (heads the remote already refused at this sha), and nothing
+batches. Every other bead stays assigned and waits. An empty WORK takes the IDLE
+path below, with no drain-ack. The marker clears when `origin/<target>` moves.
+
 **The batch (merge_batch_max = {{merge_batch_max}}).** With the default of 1, or
 a placeholder left unrendered, the block batches nothing and prints at most an
 INFO line: this is the single-bead lane, unchanged. With a larger value, and a
